column1:
3:2|LORD, I have heard the report about you;
I am afraid.
LORD, bring your work to life in these years;
make it known in these years.
In your turmoil, remember compassion.|Retains repeated years and the appeal for compassion within divine upheaval.

3:6|He stands and measures the earth;
he looks, and nations leap in alarm.
Ancient mountains shatter;
age-old hills bow down.
His paths are everlasting.|Follows measures rather than silently changing the verb to shakes; preserves ancient/everlasting contrasts.
